2026-09-27T09:10:27.4323408Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4323614Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4323898Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4324164Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4324254Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4324500Z ================
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4324626Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4324786Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4325140Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4325360Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4325474Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4325738Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4325912Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4326050Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4326459Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4326815Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4327516Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4328030Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4328131Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4328894Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4329479Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4329743Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4330033Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4330411Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4330502Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4330687Z ========
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4330796Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4332049Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4333352Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4417047Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4418065Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4420201Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4421273Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4422175Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4422881Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4423645Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4423860Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4424248Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4424501Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4426304Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4428355Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4430031Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4431573Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:10:27.4431943Z 
